+# Research — project-wide pytest suite for python-multimodule
+
+## Target inventory
+- `analytics/stats.py` — `mean(values)` (empty -> ValueError) and `percentile(values, p)`
+  (empty -> ValueError, p outside 0..100 -> ValueError, sorts input, index = round(p/100 * (n-1))).
+- `analytics/window.py` — `RateWindow(capacity)` (capacity <= 0 -> ValueError), `add` with
+  capacity rollover (oldest sample dropped), `average`/`peak` (empty -> RuntimeError).
+- `textkit/slug.py` — `slugify(value, max_length=48)` collapses/trims non-alphanumeric runs,
+  truncates over-length slugs and strips a trailing hyphen, `max_length <= 0` -> ValueError.
+
+## Testability
+- Pure functions and an in-memory class; no I/O, no time, no external services.
+- `pyproject.toml` sets `pythonpath = ["."]` and `testpaths = ["tests"]`, so tests under
+  `tests/` import `analytics.*` and `textkit.*` directly and run with `pytest`.
+
+## Scope
+- Project-wide but bounded to the three named modules. No new production code.
